{title: He Keeps Me Singing}
{artist: Luther B. Bridgers}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Upbeat}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: he-keeps-me-singing.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (He_Keeps_Me_Singing-He_Keeps_Me_Singing-Melody_of_Love)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]There's within my heart a [A7]melody
[D7]Jesus whispers sweet and [G]low,__[D7]__
[G]"Fear not, I am with thee, [A7]peace, be still,"
[D7]In all of life's ebb and [G]flow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [D7]Jesus, sweetest name I [G]know,
[G]Fills my every [Am]longing, [D7]keeps me singing as I [G]go.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]All my life was wrecked by [A7]sin and strife,
[D7]Discord filled my heart with [G]pain,__[D7]__
[G]Jesus swept across the [A7]broken strings,
[D7]Stirred the slumbering chords a[G]gain.__[D7]__[G]__[Am]__[D7]__[G]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Feasting on the riches [A7]of His grace,
[D7]Resting ’neath His sheltering [G]wing,__[D7]__
[G]Always looking on His [A7]smiling face,
[D7]That is why I shout and [G]sing.__[D7]__[G]__[Am]__[D7]__[G]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Though sometimes He leads through [A7]waters deep,
[D7]Trials fall across the [G]way,__[D7]__
[G]Though sometimes the path seems [A7]rough and steep,
[D7]See His footprints all the [G]way.__[D7]__[G]__[Am]__[D7]__[G]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Soon He’s coming back to [A7]welcome me,
[D7]Far beyond the starry [G]sky;__[D7]__
[G]I shall wing my flight to [A7]worlds unknown,
[D7]I shall reign with Him on [G]high.__[D7]__[G]__[Am]__[D7]__[G]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
